From fe35c73ea5e69f8e4cde94a47557df01e8cf29bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:58:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 338/371] pirates: random land bosses on, as the original
 shipped (bulbs gap 5, AI only)

The enemy spawner's own default is on (DistributedEnemySpawnerAI: config.GetBool('want-random-bosses', True)); only
the fan repo's config/dev.prc set it off. dev.prc line 23 #f -> #t. The AI loads general.prc, dev.prc, server.prc
(server-ctl passes no config list) and nothing else sets the flag, so the AI now sees it on. A spawned land enemy has
a small chance to come up as the named boss of its kind (bigger, tougher, name over its head); same enemy slots, so
no extra enemies.

AI restart only; no UberDOG, no client publish (the client never reads the flag). Tests: test_random_bosses.py live
FAIL (AI sees False) -> patched PASS; sim_bosses.py (the spawner's own pick code, 20,060 draws): off 0 bosses, on 156
(0.78%) across 34 kinds, 37 boss types all build, PASS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 config/dev.prc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/config/dev.prc b/config/dev.prc
index 11ff88a..0563958 100644
--- a/config/dev.prc
+++ b/config/dev.prc
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@ cache-quest-step #t
 want-townfolk #t
 want-enemies #t
 want-animals #t
-want-random-bosses #f
+want-random-bosses #t
 
 # Hotkeys:
 want-dev-hotkeys #f
